\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Radiative polarization build-up following $P(t) = P_{\mathrm  {eq}}\left (1 - e^{-t/\tau _{\mathrm  {ST}}}\right )$ [Eq.~13]. The ideal Sokolov--Ternov asymptote $8/(5\sqrt  {3}) \approx 92.4\%$ [Eq.~14] is shown alongside a representative reduced equilibrium, as occurs in a real lattice where field inhomogeneity, including that of the polarization wigglers, lowers the attainable value. At $t = \tau _{\mathrm  {ST}}$ the polarization reaches $(1 - e^{-1}) \approx 63\%$ of its equilibrium value.}}{4}{}}
